<section id="install" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">A Go, ready in three steps</h2>
  <ol class="steps-grid steps-grid--sequence">
    <li>
      <h3>Order.</h3>
      <p>Order a LilyGO T-Echo or T-Echo Plus, in 868&nbsp;MHz with the BME280 barometer.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Install.</h3>
      <p>Connect the device by USB-C and press <span class="mono">RST</span> twice. Copy the .uf2 file from the <a href="https://github.com/fcatuhe/skyblip/releases">latest release</a> to the <span class="mono">TECHOBOOT</span> drive that appears.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Activate.</h3>
      <p><%= link_to "Activate it", briefing_activation_path %> over Bluetooth in Chrome or Edge, then confirm activation with two presses on the device. Until then, a new Go neither transmits nor receives. Briefing then lets you set your <a href="#type">aircraft type</a> and callsign. Both are optional. If the device needs a GPS position before saving them, it tells you. You can change both later in the device&rsquo;s menu or from <%= link_to "Briefing", briefing_root_path %>.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section id="install-bravo" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">A Bravo, ready in three steps</h2>
  <ol class="steps-grid steps-grid--sequence">
    <li>
      <h3>Order.</h3>
      <p>Order a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Install.</h3>
      <p>Hold the button, plug in the USB-C cable and keep holding until the LED turns white, about 3 seconds. A drive named <span class="mono">X1</span> appears. First, copy <span class="mono">CURRENT.UF2</span> from it to your computer. Dragging that file back onto the drive restores Meshtastic. Then copy the .uf2 file of the <a href="https://github.com/fcatuhe/skyblip/releases">latest skyBlip Bravo release</a> onto the <span class="mono">X1</span> drive.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Set up.</h3>
      <p>Bravo needs no activation. In <%= link_to "Briefing", briefing_root_path %>, set your aircraft&rsquo;s ICAO address so your own transponder is left out.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="signature">
    Later updates for both devices come from <%= link_to "Briefing", briefing_root_path %>
    over Bluetooth. Each one is approved on the device: on the Go&rsquo;s screen, or with two presses on Bravo.
    The same file works on the T&#8209;Echo and the T&#8209;Echo Plus. For now,
    only development versions are published for both devices.
  </p>
</section>

