<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Your questions, answered</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Why the BME280 barometer?</summary>
      <p>It is required for skyBlip conformity. Some T-Echo units are sold without it: pick the version that lists it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does the X1 work with skyBlip?</summary>
      <p>Yes, with the skyBlip Bravo firmware. It ships with Meshtastic, which receives no ADS-B. <%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "About Bravo", anchor: "status" %>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need to open or solder the device?</summary>
      <p>No. The device comes assembled. The firmware installs over the USB cable.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do updates cost anything?</summary>
      <p>No. The firmware and its updates are free, and will stay free.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I update from an iPhone?</summary>
      <p>
        No. The update page needs Web Bluetooth, the browser&rsquo;s Bluetooth feature, which Safari does not support.
        Use Chrome or Edge on a computer or on Android. Installing over a USB
        cable from a computer needs no browser.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What if I want to go back?</summary>
      <p>
        The skyBlip firmware leaves the T-Echo&rsquo;s factory startup program (bootloader)
        unchanged. You can reinstall the other software available for the device as
        before.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="cta-pair">
    <p>Not decided yet?</p>
    <div class="cta-pair-buttons">
